latest_plan = "Based on the reflection, here's a detailed step-by-step plan to solve the challenge:\n\n1. Analyze the input grid:\n   a. Identify all non-black shapes in the grid\n   b. For each shape, record its color, size (number of cells), bounding box, and centroid\n   c. Categorize shapes into initial top, middle, and bottom sections based on their centroid's y-coordinate\n\n2. Calculate space allocation:\n   a. Compute the total area of shapes in each initial section (top, middle, bottom)\n   b. Allocate rows in the output grid proportionally to these areas, with a minimum of 1 row per section\n\n3. Sort and group shapes:\n   a. Within each section, group shapes by color\n   b. Sort shapes within each color group by size (descending)\n   c. Sort color groups by the total size of shapes in the group (descending)\n\n4. Initialize the output grid:\n   a. Create a new grid of the same dimensions as the input, filled with black (0)\n\n5. Place shapes in the output grid:\n   a. Start with the top section, then middle, then bottom\n   b. For each section:\n      i. Begin with the largest color group\n      ii. Place shapes from left to right, top to bottom within the section\n      iii. If a shape doesn't fit in its original section:\n           - Try the adjacent section (middle for top/bottom, top then bottom for middle)\n           - If still no fit, try the remaining section\n      iv. When placing a shape, align it to the top-left of the available space\n      v. Move to the next color group and repeat\n\n6. Optimize placement:\n   a. After initial placement, identify any large gaps\n   b. If a gap is larger than any unplaced shape, try to move a shape from another section to fill it\n   c. Adjust the position of shapes within their color groups to center the group if space allows\n\n7. Balance the grid:\n   a. Calculate the density of shapes in each third of the grid\n   b. If one third is significantly emptier than the others, try to move shapes from denser areas to balance\n\n8. Final adjustments:\n   a. Ensure all shapes are placed\n   b. If any shapes couldn't be placed, expand the grid vertically and repeat steps 5-7\n   c. Trim any empty rows at the bottom of the grid\n\n9. Return the final output grid\n\nThis plan addresses the key aspects of the challenge:\n- It maintains the general structure of top, middle, and bottom sections while allowing flexibility\n- It groups shapes by color and prioritizes larger shapes and larger color groups\n- It efficiently uses space by allowing shapes to move between sections when necessary\n- It includes steps for optimizing and balancing the final layout\n\nThis approach should be able to handle all the given examples and test cases, as well as generalize to new cases. The flexibility in section allocation and shape placement allows it to adapt to different input configurations while still maintaining the core principles of the challenge."
